#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/029_herbs_for_the_lakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Healers dried herbs in bundles under the roof, to have them all winter."
msgstr "Целители сушили травы пучками под крышей, чтобы их хватило на всю зиму."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Mill Turns"
msgstr "Мельница крутится"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The harvest is in, and the mill wheel turns day and night! But the farmers are slow. Bring me six "
"crates of grain to grind."
msgstr ""
"Урожай собран, и мельничное колесо крутится днём и ночью! Но крестьяне не торопятся. "
"{crew|Привези|Привези|Привезите} мне шесть ящиков зерна на помол."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six crates! Listen to the stones grind. Bjarne says hello, and here is your share."
msgstr ""
"Шесть ящиков! {crew|Послушай|Послушай|Послушайте}, как мелют жернова. Бьярне передаёт привет, а "
"вот {crew|твоя|твоя|ваша} доля."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/030_the_mill_turns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Most vikings ground their grain by hand with two stones; a water mill was a wonder."
msgstr "Большинство викингов мололи зерно вручную двумя камнями; водяная мельница была чудом."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A Henhouse Full"
msgstr "Полный курятник"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Eggs sell so well! Let us have six hens. Buy hens at the market in Kråkhamn or the farm of "
"Frosttorp, and bring them home."
msgstr ""
"Яйца так хорошо продаются! {crew|Давай|Давай|Давайте} заведём шесть кур. {crew|Купи|Купи|Купите} "
"кур на рынке в Крокхамне или на хуторе во Фросторпе и {crew|привези|привези|привезите} их домой."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Six hens! Cluck, cluck, scratch, scratch. Do not forget: they eat grain."
msgstr "Шесть кур! Ко-ко-ко, шкряб-шкряб. Не {crew|забывай|забывай|забывайте}: они едят зерно."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/031_a_henhouse_full/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking hens were small and laid fewer eggs than ours, but every farm had some."
msgstr "Куры викингов были маленькими и неслись реже наших, но они были на каждой ферме."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey Cakes"
msgstr "Медовые пряники"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We want to sell honey cakes on the market! But we have no oven. Bring honey and grain to your "
"grandmother; she bakes them overnight, and you bring us the cakes."
msgstr ""
"Мы хотим продавать на рынке медовые пряники! Но у нас нет печи. {crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} мёд "
"и зерно своей бабушке; она испечёт их за ночь, а {crew|ты привезёшь|ты привезёшь|вы привезёте} нам"
" пряники."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Honey! Now the grain."
msgstr "Мёд! Теперь зерно."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "I bake them tonight. Come for them in the morning!"
msgstr "Испеку их сегодня вечером. {crew|Приезжай|Приезжай|Приезжайте} за ними утром!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Still warm. Do not eat them all on the way!"
msgstr "Ещё тёплые. Не {crew|съешь|съешь|съешьте} все по дороге!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "They smell so good! Everybody comes to our stall. Here, half the silver is yours."
msgstr "Как они пахнут! Все идут к нашему прилавку. Вот, половина серебра — {crew|твоя|твоя|ваша}."

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Cakes"
msgstr "Пряники"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
#. salt|{count} crates of salt}'
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}"
msgstr ""
"{count|корзина медовых пряников|{count} корзины медовых пряников|{count} корзин медовых пряников}"

#. the thing '{count|a basket of honey cakes|{count} baskets of honey cakes}' for {thing@acc} in the
#. translations: the accusative (the direct object), e.g. 'бочку эля', 'bačvu piva'; leave it empty
#. if it is the same as the plain translation
#: data/missions/032_honey_cakes/mission.json
#, fuzzy
