#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The nights grow long. The guests of the autumn feast need light: bring me tar for torches, two "
"pots from Ekvik, and two crates of flax for the wicks."
msgstr ""
"Ночи становятся длинными. Гостям осеннего пира нужен свет: {crew|привези|привези|привезите} мне "
"смолу для факелов, два горшка из Эквика, и два ящика льна для фитилей."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar for torches? They burn bright and long."
msgstr "Смола для факелов? Они горят ярко и долго."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Tar and flax: now my torches will light up the whole bay!"
msgstr "Смола и лён: теперь мои факелы осветят весь залив!"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/045_torches_for_the_dark/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Viking torches were sticks wrapped in flax or cloth, soaked in tar or fat."
msgstr "Факелы викингов были палками, обмотанными льном или тканью и пропитанными смолой или жиром."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
