msgid "Hedda the goat"
msgstr "козу Хедду"

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/053_the_lame_goat/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Goats climb anything: rocks, roofs, and sometimes boats."
msgstr "Козы залезают куда угодно: на скалы, на крыши, а иногда и в лодки."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley in Spring"
msgstr "Весенний ячмень"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The fields are dry: time to sow! Plant barley, and while it grows, sell two crates of eggs to Orm "
"in Hallvik to buy more seed."
msgstr ""
"Поля высохли: пора сеять! {crew|Посади|Посади|Посадите} ячмень, а пока он растёт, "
"{crew|продай|продай|продайте} два ящика яиц Орму в Халльвике, чтобы купить ещё семян."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The barley is sown. Now the sun and the rain do the work."
msgstr "Ячмень посеян. Теперь работают солнце и дождь."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eggs! I make my famous egg cake. Here, good silver for good eggs."
msgstr "Яйца! Испеку свой знаменитый яичный пирог. Вот, хорошее серебро за хорошие яйца."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/054_barley_in_spring/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Barley was the most important grain of the north: for bread, porridge and ale."
msgstr "Ячмень был главным зерном севера: для хлеба, каши и эля."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "The Great Hold"
msgstr "Большой трюм"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Now we make your boat great! Ten planks from Frosttorp, three crates of tools, and 30 silver. Then"
" she takes two more crates. Ten planks are more than you can carry at once."
msgstr ""
"Теперь сделаем {crew|твою|твою|вашу} лодку большой! Десять досок из Фросторпа, три ящика "
"инструментов и 30 серебра. Тогда в неё войдут ещё два ящика. Десять досок за один раз не увезти."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Planks again? Bjarne is building you a ship!"
msgstr "Опять доски? Бьярне строит {crew|тебе|тебе|вам} целый корабль!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Iron for the rivets. Now my wages."
msgstr "Железо для заклёпок. Теперь моя плата."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Two more crates! And go and see Signe in Ekvik: she builds real ships, and my crates go with you "
"into any of them."
msgstr ""
"Ещё два ящика! А теперь {crew|загляни|загляни|загляните} к Сигне в Эквик: она строит настоящие "
"корабли, и мои ящики переедут с {crew|тобой|тобой|вами} в любой из них."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/055_the_great_hold/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "A knarr, the cargo ship of the vikings, could carry the load of twenty boats."
msgstr "Кнорр, грузовой корабль викингов, мог везти груз двадцати лодок."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bjørn's Salt Run"
msgstr "Соль Бьёрна"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"My boat leaks, and the fishers of Ekvik wait for salt! Take eight sacks for me from here to Ekvik."
" Your new hold is just right."
msgstr ""
"Моя лодка протекает, а рыбаки Эквика ждут соль! {crew|Отвези|Отвези|Отвезите} за меня восемь "
"мешков отсюда в Эквик. {crew|Твой|Твой|Ваш} новый трюм — как раз то, что надо."

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Bjørn's salt, brought by you? Then I pay you, not him. Ha!"
msgstr ""
"Соль Бьёрна, {crew|а привёз её ты|а привезла её ты|а привезли её вы}? Тогда я плачу "
"{crew|тебе|тебе|вам}, а не ему. Ха!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Eight sacks of the best salt from the sea. Keep them dry!"
msgstr "Восемь мешков лучшей морской соли. {crew|Береги|Береги|Берегите} их от воды!"

#. a thing of a task, under its crate: at most 10 letters
#: data/missions/056_bjorns_salt_run/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Salt"
msgstr "Соль"

#. a thing of a task; {count|...|...} picks the form for the number {count} (one, then the others;
#. see the Plural-Forms of this file for how many forms your language has), e.g., '{count|a crate of
