#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale for Two Inns"
msgstr "Эль для двух трактиров"

#. what the giver of a task asks, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Both inns ran dry at the same time! Six barrels for Gudrun in Vargvik and six for Orm in Hallvik. "
"With twelve crates of room, you can do it in one trip!"
msgstr ""
"В обоих трактирах эль кончился одновременно! Шесть бочек для Гудрун в Варгвике и шесть для Орма в "
"Халльвике. С трюмом на двенадцать ящиков {crew|ты справишься|ты справишься|вы справитесь} за один "
"рейс!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Ale! The guests cheer. Thank you!"
msgstr "Эль! Гости ликуют. Спасибо!"

#. what a person says, at most 6 lines
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "At last! I thought I must serve water. Here, silver for you and for Knut."
msgstr ""
"Наконец-то! Я уж думал, придётся подавать воду. Вот серебро для {crew|тебя|тебя|вас} и для Кнута."

#. a fun fact at the end of a task, 2 short sentences
#: data/missions/077_ale_for_two_inns/mission.json
#, fuzzy
msgid "Everybody drank weak ale every day: it was safer than water from the lake."
msgstr "Все каждый день пили слабый эль: это было безопаснее, чем озёрная вода."

#. the title of a task, also on its card (a button): a few words, at most two short lines
#: data/missions/078_the_sleepy_hens/mission.json
